{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790973988,"nonce":"WJsfKf0yIcaeprBMBneGWG6881g=","title":"Evaluation order, switch subjects, exceptions and float remainder: second triage round","message":"Triage of 32 wrong-number rows (batches Q-T). Fixed here:\n\n- Every evaluation of `throw` stored the stack trace into a `stack` slot found BY NAME across all classes (haxe.Exception's slot 3), so throwing any class without that field wrote past the end of the object (heap overflow), and a null exception faulted. The owner must now be the thrown class or an ancestor, and null is skipped.\n- A release placed after `_setjmp` in its block ran twice when an exception longjmped back (double free, SIGTRAP in malloc on two consecutive try/catch). insert_free now keeps releases of values defined before the setjmp ahead of it, or drops them when the value is still read after it. 3cc9e60.\n- The last typed catch clause was unconditional and an unmatched exception was swallowed: a typed clause is now tested (classes through their hierarchy, basic types by id), with the old fallback kept only for types that cannot be tested; with no finally, an unmatched exception is rethrown. Thrown and caught types compare through typedefs and as an abstract's underlying type. Issue7653. With a finally block the unmatched path still falls through.\n- Cranelift lowered float `%` as floored modulo; Haxe truncates like fmod (LLVM `frem`, the interpreter). Issue4068 (its remaining failure is b68d33d), TestOps gets further.\n- `case [1, 1] | [1, 0]:` skipped the destructuring guard and compared fresh arrays by address. Issue2633, Issue5873.\n- A switch subject was evaluated once per case test (value-matching chain) or once per pattern binding (guard desugar). The subject is evaluated once; an array-literal subject binds each element to its own local. Issue5242, Issue9938 kept.\n- `for (i in a...b)` re-read `b` every iteration. Issue4702.\n- Quoted object literal keys kept their escape sequences. Issue5000.\n- `indexOf`/`lastIndexOf` did not clamp the start position, and `lastIndexOf`'s -1 \"from the end\" sentinel collided with an explicit negative start. Issue5271.\n- Object literal fields were evaluated in sorted (layout) order. Issue7531.\n- An abstract method whose body is a switch with patterns was inlined as value equality, losing captures and `|` alternatives. Issue5392, Issue9667.\n\nGate: 796 -\u003e 806, 0 lost; TestOps moved WRONG_ANSWER -\u003e CRASH (it reached the crash it already had after its first assertion stopped failing).\n\nUnfixed causes from this round: 3cc9e60..b68d33d (18 issues) and comments on 4c1d8fb, a296dc2, 4b5a733.","files":null}]}